   121	// toolchainWalk collects the canonical record set. It reproduces exactly what
   122	// fs.WalkDir over os.Root.FS() produced — the same entries, the same
   123	// name-sorted visit order, and therefore the same error precedence — but it
   124	// takes each entry's Lstat through a handle scoped to the directory the entry
   125	// lives in instead of re-resolving the entry's whole root-relative path one
   126	// component at a time. That Lstat is the only step this saves; every
   127	// step whose result nothing later re-resolves stays anchored at GOROOT:
   128	//
   129	//   - each directory is listed through a handle opened by its full root-relative
   130	//     path, exactly as fs.ReadDir opened it;
   131	//   - an entry the listing types as a directory is Lstat-ed by its full path,
   132	//     because the digest phase never revisits a directory record, and it is
   133	//     descended by its full path, because fs.WalkDir took both decisions from
   134	//     the listed entry and failed closed when the path stopped being one;
   135	//   - a link's target and resolvability are read from the root, because a link
   136	//     target is validated against GOROOT and not against its own directory —
   137	//     the accepted RC4 vector contains "pkg/tool-link" -> "../bin/go", which
   138	//     resolves inside the root but outside its own directory.
   139	//
   140	// What remains scoped is the Lstat of files and links, and both are re-checked
   280		}
